      "section": "Cells in the image",
      "order": 3,
      "alignment": "left",
      "vertical_alignment": "top",
      "body": "One mcquant table (nf-core/mcmicro) of two tonsil images: per cell, eight marker intensities, the centroid in image pixels and the segmentation morphology. On the left, spatial_cells draws each cell in its image's own frame (y down from the top-left, one image at a time), at the size of its area, coloured by cell type or by a marker picked from the panel, with the colour clipped to the 1st and 99th percentiles. On the right, an embedding of X_centroid and Y_centroid: the same cells, upside down (its y axis runs up), both images stacked in one frame, every cell one fixed-size dot. Pick a sample on the left to compare like with like; a lasso in either tile marks its cells in the other.\n",
      "surface": "none",
      "accent": null,
      "logo": null,
      "logo_dark": null,
      "wf_tag": "python/advanced_viz_demo"
    },
